        "original_id": "0cdaac8a-06a4-52ea-a673-14bd2c6a5eaa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Enzo Ferrari, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola\n- Companies: Ferrari, Fiat S.p.A., Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV\n- Organizations: Confindustria, FIEG, FerrariWorld\n- Products: Ferrari Ascari\n- Concepts: automotive industry, holding companies, mergers, competition judges\n\nFacts:\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was born on 31 August 1947 and is an Italian businessman.\n- Luca Cordero di Montezemolo was formerly Chairman of Ferrari and Fiat S.p.A. and was President of Confindustria and FIEG.\n- Fiat S.p.A., short for Fabbrica Italiana Automobili Torino, was an Italian holding company whose original and core activities were in the automotive industry.\n- On 29 January 2014, Fiat S.p.A. announced that it would merge into the new Netherlands-based holding company Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV, and the merger took place before the end of 2014.\n- Fiat Chrysler Automobiles NV succeeded Fiat S.p.A.\n- Judges for the Ferrari Ascari competition included Luca Cordero di Montezemolo, Piero Ferrari, Jean Todt, Amedeo Felisa, Massimo Fumarola, Pininfarina, and more than 22,000 users of FerrariWorld's website.\n- Piero Ferrari is the second and only living son of Enzo Ferrari.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
